to apply for larger funding opportunities\\nThe grants:\\nSupport high-quality clinical or translational research in hematology\\nLast for a period of two years\\nCan provide a total award of up to €300,000 for the whole consortium\\nEligibility\\nEvery principal investigator (PI) must be an EHA member.\\nAll PIs must be conducting high-quality clinical or translational research. Basic and/or translational researchers can also be included, but the general focus of the project must remain clinical and translational.\\nAll PIs must be independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents in Europe.\\nEach consortium must include at least three PIs operating in at least three different countries in Europe.\\nAt least one of the PIs must operate in of the following countries: Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Croatia, Estonia, Georgia, Hungary, Kosovo, Latvia, Lithuania, Moldova, Montenegro, North Macedonia, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Serbia, Slovak Republic, Slovenia, Türkiye, Ukraine.\\nAt least one of the PIs must be a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting in\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-c60022ff9847a5c52747af0c\", \"title\": \"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4126, \"end\": 4170, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 44}, {\"start\": 4267, \"end\": 4324, \"excerpt_start\": 45, \"excerpt_end\": 102}, {\"start\": 4437, \"end\": 5936, \"excerpt_start\": 103, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · May 16, 2025\\nMay 16, 2025\\nShare\\nWhat is precision hematology?\\nPrecision hematology is an integrated approach to diagnosing and treating blood disorders—particularly hematologic malignancies—by leveraging detailed molecular, genetic, and functional information about each patient’s disease.\\nIt matches therapies more precisely to individual patients by uniting innovative clinical trial designs with cutting-edge diagnostics, such as:\\nAdvanced imaging\\nGenetic profiling\\nDrug-sensitivity testing\\nThis field brings together physicians, scientists, and other key stakeholders across preclinical, translational, and clinical research. Through this collaboration, precision hematology aims to:\\nAccelerate the discovery of new treatment strategies\\nRefine therapeutic decision-making\\nImprove outcomes for patients with blood cancers\\nOur program’s goals\\nOur Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program is designed to promote innovative concepts for diagnostics and innovative clinical trial designs which will feed into the clinical application of precision hematology.\\nThe goal of the program is to create a European regulatory framework for precision hematology. By increasing awareness and providing education, guidelines, and policies, we can improve access to:\\nDiagnostics\\nClinical research\\nTreatment in malignant hematology\\nUseful materials\\nEHA Position Paper on Personalized Treatment for Hematologic Diseases\\nPrecision Medicine in Hematology in 2021: Definitions, Tools, Perspectives, and Open Questions\\nIn Vitro Diagnostic Medical\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-ece509e1ea7055ce41222f0b\", \"title\": \"Non-EHA funding opportunities - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Non-EHA funding opportunities - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4130, \"end\": 4185, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 55}, {\"start\": 4407, \"end\": 4690, \"excerpt_start\": 56, \"excerpt_end\": 339}, {\"start\": 5152, \"end\": 5172, \"excerpt_start\": 340, \"excerpt_end\": 360}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n1 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nOn th